<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baghdad Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Central Treaty Organization, CENTO</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> Pact was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> defensive alliance formed in 1955 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and the United Kingdom, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> closely associated. It aimed to contain Soviet influence in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>. After the 1958 revolution Iraq withdrew in 1959, and the alliance was renamed the Central Treaty Organization, which was dissolved in 1979.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact.jpg" alt="Baghdad Pact" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Little Professor · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cento_zoom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
